+## Genuine search for a new front (and why each candidate was rejected)
+
+Per the standing mandate, an empty curator response is not proof that research is
+complete. I examined concrete, literature- and obstacle-grounded candidates:
+
+- **Cremer (2026) finite proof-carrying DAG for 7th-of-16 selection → uniform
+  sorting certificate.** The authoritative cert frontier already classifies this
+  as a finite selection precedent with no all-n bridge; finite-to-uniform
+  transfer is exactly the open framed-certificate completeness problem already
+  curated (`framed-dag-polynomial-alln`, `polynomial-framed-certificate-np`,
+  `optimal-tree-np-certificate`). Repeating it would be duplicate work.
+- **SETH / fine-grained conditional lower bound for exact `S(n)`.** `problem.md`
+  flags a fixed-polynomial lower bound for a single natural number sequence as
+  having no known technique; `SORT-BOUND-U` is a sparse tally language with no
+  P/SETH-hardness under standard reductions (`selfreducible-minimax-p-hard`,
+  `tally-np-membership-collapse`, `fixed-poly-time-lower-bound` already closed
+  this direction negatively). Unsuitable.
+- **P-recursive / D-finite recurrence for the sequence `S(n)`.** Finitary prefix
+  fitting can only refute low-order recurrences, not prove absence, and the
+  structural recurrence obligation is already covered by
+  `root-composition-exact-recurrence` and the automatic-sequence barriers
+  (`k-regular-sorting-number`). Not a decisive falsifiable all-n question.
+- **Adaptive-vs-oblivious network gap.** Settled: `adaptive-network-size-gap`
+  proves `N(n)-S(n) = omega(1)` (gap exceeds n/4 for large n).
+
